    "reading": "Contemporaneous cross-fold association is strong and survives fold separation, so it is a genuine hotel-quarter quality signal, not same-review mechanics. The LEAD specification (aspect change -> next-quarter rating change) is indistinguishable from zero, so these data do not support 'improving aspect X raises later ratings'.",
    "note": "Observational. Fold separation removes same-review mechanical coupling but does not randomise hotel quality, and mean reversion in hotel quality depresses the lead coefficient. Outcome is guest RATING, not revenue: no price, room-night or cost fields exist in this dataset.",
    "attenuation_note": "Treatment is measured with sampling error independent of the outcome error (classical errors-in-variables), so |beta| is biased toward zero: estimates are lower bounds in magnitude."
